# OTRv4+ shipped I2P name aliases.
#
# THIS FILE MAPS NO NAME TO A DESTINATION, ON PURPOSE.
# ----------------------------------------------------
# A short `.i2p` name is resolved by the ROUTER, with SAM NAMING LOOKUP,
# every time. The router's address book is the authority for what a name
# means now; this client does not second-guess it with a shipped address.
#
# This file used to map the project's server name to its b32, and was
# consulted before the router. When the server was recreated under the same
# name, every client quietly rewrote the name to the OLD destination and never
# asked the router at all -- a newly created server entered by name was
# unreachable (device report, 2026-09-28). No destination is shipped here now,
# and no build depends on one.
#
# ~/.otrv4plus/i2p_hosts (Termux) is still read, but only for a name the
# router answers KEY_NOT_FOUND for, and its use is announced. The Android app
# does not read either file.
#
# Name lines, if ever added again, use:   name.i2p = <52 chars>.b32.i2p
#
# Retired destinations.  A b32 is NEVER silently redirected -- an address
# given in full is used as given -- but if it is listed here the client can
# say that it moved and name the current form.
#
# Format:  retired <old 52 chars>.b32.i2p <name it moved to>
